 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Committed revisions reach browsers over sockets the project runs itself. Five-second HTTPS polling was rejected for its repeated reads, seconds of lag, and a polling loop in every browser. A hosted realtime service was rejected for its recurring fees and provider coupling. The accepted cost is owning connection capacity for 800 browsers plus reconnect and catch-up logic.
